id: pm-linear-nvt5
title: Add opt-in --atomic to linear import/sync via SDK commitItemMutations
description: "Atomic, crash-resumable, multi-agent-safe bulk-write path for pm-linear. Mirrors the merged pm-github reference. Companion tracker: pm-cli-website-c9u0 at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli-companion (parent epic pm-cli-website-s4wz)."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-21T12:39:12.520Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-21T16:09:16.974Z"
assignee: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
notes[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-21T12:39:58.574Z",pi-agent,"DESIGN DECISIONS:\n- Stable item id keyed on Linear issue identifier (e.g. ENG-123), the most stable human-meaningful external key, never fetch order. deriveAtomicItemId hashes lowercased team + identifier through normalizeItemId.\n- Transaction id fingerprints lowercased team + canonical entries sorted by the stable identifier + the exact ordered BulkItemMutation plan. A changed id_prefix or provenance match yields a fresh journal; a reordered retry resumes the same one.\n- Mutation plan: create+update upsert for new/deterministic-id items (same plan on recovery when provenance scan finds the deterministic id); update(+close) for legacy matches at a different id. close is a separate mutation preserving a reason and is independently reversible.\n- Compensation: createCompensation='delete' for creates; SDK version-restores updates+closes. On AggregateError/compensation-failed -> warn tracker MAY be partial + same-transaction recovery path; normal SDK compensation -> no new partial state; WorkspaceTransactionInterruptedError -> resumable.\n- Byte-compatible default: non-atomic per-issue spawnSync path is UNCHANGED. --atomic --dry-run shares the atomic prep/matching path (fetches issues, reports create/update/skip counts) and NEVER commits; the non-atomic --dry-run stays fully offline (GraphQL request preview).\n- All-skipped non-dry atomic import throws the SAME error shape as legacy (CommandError 'Imported 0 issue(s); N failed.', exitCode GENERIC_FAILURE) BEFORE commit.\n- Exported CommandError/EXIT_CODE/LinearIssue/syncLinearIssues (+SyncRunDependencies test seams) mirroring pm-github; package.json peerDep >=2026.7.20, devDep ^2026.7.20 (latest published with commitItemMutations; ^2026.7.21 not yet on npm)."
  "2026-07-21T12:40:15.159Z",pi-agent,"QUALITY GATE: npm run release:check PASSED.\n- typecheck (tsc --noEmit): clean\n- build (tsc): clean\n- npm test: 61 tests pass / 0 fail (51 smoke + 10 new atomic)\n- audit:prod: 0 vulnerabilities\n- pack:dry-run: ok (9 files, 50.7 kB)\n- changelog:check: up to date (no regeneration needed)\n\nAtomic test coverage (test/atomic.test.ts, 10 tests):\n1. mid-run failure -> reverse compensation restores created/updated/closed items (failed batch deletes every create; mixed batch restores updates+closes)\n2. resume idempotence -> re-running same fetched set recovers SAME transaction, 0 duplicates\n3. reordered-retry stability -> shuffled fetch order yields SAME transaction id & item ids\n4. --atomic --dry-run -> shared prep path, correct counts (1 import/1 update/1 skip), NO SDK commit call\n5. all-skipped non-dry atomic import -> throws legacy error shape (CommandError, 'Imported 0 issue(s); 1 failed'), before commit\n6. transaction id changes when a mutation target changes (id, id_prefix, status)\nPlus: incomplete compensation reported as partial+resumable; end-to-end update+close commit through the real SDK against a live tracker."
  "2026-07-21T12:55:11.201Z",claude-orchestrator,"Orchestrator independent verification (2026-07-21): re-ran the full release gate — 61/61 tests pass, 0 prod vulnerabilities, changelog current, pack clean. Reviewed the atomic design against the merged pm-github reference: deriveAtomicTransactionId hashes team + identifier-sorted canonical entries + exact ordered mutation plan; deriveAtomicItemId keys on the stable Linear identifier (linear-<teamToken>-<identifier>), never fetch order; importLinearAtomic sorts entries by identifier BEFORE building the plan (order-independence). Ran an independent live harness on the built dist/index.js + REAL SDK against throwaway workspaces: (A) atomic import of 5 realistic entries (2 closed) -> 5 items, txn linear-import-333458e94167573e; re-run recovered the SAME transaction, 0 new, 5 items total (no duplicates); (B) SHUFFLED fetch order through importLinearAtomic -> IDENTICAL transaction id and identical managed item ids. Local greptile CLI produced empty output (known flakiness) -> relying on the PR-time Greptile app + CodeRabbit/Sourcery/cubic/semgrep. Ready to push + PR."
  "2026-07-21T15:55:36.079Z",claude-orchestrator,"Bot-review hardening round (PR #36): (1) gemini-high + no reopen churn — removed shared status field; create seeds open, update omits status, close owns the closed transition; (2) gemini-high + greptile-P1 — all-filtered batch now returns a successful zero-sync result before touching the SDK (matches legacy path; unblocks cron/CI); (3) greptile-P1 — settings read fault now throws CommandError instead of forking id_prefix to 'pm-' (protects transaction/journal identity so resume can't duplicate items); (4) greptile-P1 — linear-sync importer now forwards --dry-run so --atomic --dry-run previews without writing. +2 tests (63 total). Functionally verified end-to-end against a real throwaway pm workspace via real SDK commitItemMutations: create/close, idempotent recovered resume, tx id stable under reorder."
  "2026-07-21T16:09:16.974Z",claude-orchestrator,"Static-analysis cleanup (DeepScan '1 new issue' on PR #36): removed genuine dead code surfaced by strict tsc (noUnusedLocals/noUnusedParameters) — the unused, unexported KNOWN_LINEAR_FIELDS const (parseFieldMap accepts any key, never referenced it) and the unused 'options' parameter on preflightLinear (2 call sites updated). Build+typecheck+63 tests green. All other analyzers clean (Greptile pass, CodeRabbit full review 0 findings, Hound pass, CI pass)."
body: ""
